00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.390
the end user, the data path.

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:02.010
The data path is
quickly to the desktop,

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:04.220
and then the desktop
pings back to the user

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:06.115
to make sure this is
happening everywhere.

00:19:06.115 --> 00:19:07.490
Now the architecture
is obviously

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:10.100
set up to be smooth
and simple to operate

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:12.590
at this level with one
person, but guess what?

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:14.180
The architecture
is actually built

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:17.270
to support thousands and
thousands and thousands

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:19.070
