in 10 different regions
around the world.

00:22:40.870 --> 00:22:44.310
We've got three GPU regions and
three desktop regions in Google

00:22:44.310 --> 00:22:46.740
Cloud, three desktop
regions in Azure,

00:22:46.740 --> 00:22:49.500
and an edge
development in Dallas.

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:52.430
All of this is already setup
as they're using it today.

00:22:52.430 --> 00:22:54.870
And as it Workspot admin,
it's easy to manage this

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:56.730
from a single pane of glass.

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:59.040
Now World Co has just
acquired a company

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:00.930
with users on the
East and West Coast,

00:23:00.930 --> 00:23:04.200
and IT gets a request to add
thousands of new cloud PCs

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:05.580
on each coast.

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:07.230
I'm going to increase
the total cloud

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:10.948
PCs of each of these east and
west resource pools to 1,000,

00:23:10.948 --> 00:23:12.990
and it's only going to
take three to four minutes

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:14.073
to provision all of these.

00:23:14.073 --> 00:23:15.450
That's crazy.

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:18.270
Now we'll increase the number
of cloud PCs in the west.

00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:21.570
And as we do, the CPU storage
and networking resources

00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:24.900
and Google Cloud, East
and West, are dynamically

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:28.590
assembled to create the new
cloud PCs and configure them

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:31.710
and ready them for their
users in the regions closest

00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:33.600
to their location.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:34.530
Excellent.

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:38.490
While that's happening, let's
look at the events feed.

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.650
The events feed captures
end user activity

00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:42.750
in near real time,
users connecting

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:45.420
from different parts of the
world from different devices.

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.310
And depending on
your requirements,

00:23:47.310 --> 00:23:49.320
we have even more
user activity that

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:52.770
can be captured and fed into
Splunk and other SIM monitoring

00:23:52.770 --> 00:23:53.730
apps.

00:23:53.730 --> 00:23:56.880
As an admin in the system
you can see my event trail.

00:23:56.880 --> 00:23:59.070
There are my actions
adding thousands

00:23:59.070 --> 00:24:02.160
of desktops in two different
parts of the world.

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:04.680
For all of these
new cloud PCs I just

00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:07.140
got a request to give them
the ability to print locally.

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:09.450
So let's make a
security change enabling

00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:11.730
printing for the whole group.

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:14.670
Scroll down here, find
the actual attribute,

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:16.050
enable printing.

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:19.230
Scroll to the bottom and hit
Save and then bang, that's it.

00:24:19.230 --> 00:24:22.890
When the users log in next time,
the new policy will be pushed,

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:26.390
and printing will be
enabled for each of them.

00:24:26.390 --> 00:24:28.310
Now I'll open up
my Workspot client

00:24:28.310 --> 00:24:29.960
running on my local machine.

00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:32.150
As an admin, I've
given myself access

00:24:32.150 --> 00:24:35.240
to all the GPU-accelerated
workstations and desktops

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:36.950
in all 10 pools.

00:24:36.950 --> 00:24:38.870
As soon as I logged
in I automatically

00:24:38.870 --> 00:24:40.340
received the new
security policy,

00:24:40.340 --> 00:24:44.880
and now I have the printing
enabled on all my desktops.

00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:48.480
Let's connect to my Windows
10 desktop in Google Cloud US

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:49.020
West.

00:24:49.020 --> 00:24:50.490
That's closest to
me, and I'm going

00:24:50.490 --> 00:24:51.870
to show you how fast it is.

00:24:51.870 --> 00:24:55.240
Takes only five to seven seconds
to connect to the desktop.

00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:57.900
I can move this window
around, this is my cloud PC.

00:24:57.900 --> 00:25:01.680
And if I click I go full screen,
I can show all of my work.

00:25:01.680 --> 00:25:03.240
So I've got a browser
open here where

00:25:03.240 --> 00:25:05.670
I'm looking at
workspot.com website.

00:25:05.670 --> 00:25:08.370
And in another tab, I've
got Workspot's YouTube page

00:25:08.370 --> 00:25:10.950
full of lots of cool
customer success videos

00:25:10.950 --> 00:25:12.450
and a whole lot more.

00:25:12.450 --> 00:25:15.250
Also down below, open up
a couple of PDF files,

00:25:15.250 --> 00:25:17.310
we've got Southland
Industries case studies

00:25:17.310 --> 00:25:19.790
and viewing an interesting
analyst report.

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:21.750
I can also manage
my files from here

00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:23.160
and share them with others.

00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:25.260
I can open up
office applications

00:25:25.260 --> 00:25:28.200
like PowerPoint and Word and
just go ahead and edit away.

00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:30.600
I can run all sorts of
browser-based or Windows

00:25:30.600 --> 00:25:34.200
10-based applications that it
might even be GPU accelerated

00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:35.880
if I need it.

00:25:35.880 --> 00:25:38.010
So if I shrink this down--

00:25:38.010 --> 00:25:40.680
remind you that this
is my cloud PC--

00:25:40.680 --> 00:25:43.620
I can go anywhere and
disconnect, close the client,

00:25:43.620 --> 00:25:46.140
and it's waiting for
me there when I return.

00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:48.870
Before we check on the progress
of the thousands of desktops

00:25:48.870 --> 00:25:50.550
we created a few
minutes ago, I'm

00:25:50.550 --> 00:25:53.700
going to show you the Workspot
Network Operations Center

00:25:53.700 --> 00:25:55.650
that our support team
is using to monitor

00:25:55.650 --> 00:25:59.490
in real time what is going on
for all users in the world.

00:25:59.490 --> 00:26:01.810
As we scroll you'll see
the yellows are warnings,

00:26:01.810 --> 00:26:04.092
greens are good, and
reds are problems.

00:26:04.092 --> 00:26:05.550
We're collecting
a few dozen pieces

00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:07.860
of information in real
time for each user

00:26:07.860 --> 00:26:10.980
and for all of our customers
everywhere in the world.

00:26:10.980 --> 00:26:13.320
We analyzed the data
across all of our customers

00:26:13.320 --> 00:26:16.170
to understand if there are
significant patterns disrupting

00:26:16.170 --> 00:26:17.370
user access.

00:26:17.370 --> 00:26:18.960
Could be an office
network making

00:26:18.960 --> 00:26:21.660
access slow for all
users at one customer,

00:26:21.660 --> 00:26:24.240
or maybe an operating system
update causing problems

00:26:24.240 --> 00:26:27.060
for all users on a
particular device, or even

00:26:27.060 --> 00:26:29.910
a region of the cloud being
unavailable to all customers

00:26:29.910 --> 00:26:32.140
in that part of the world.

00:26:32.140 --> 00:26:33.930
Now we'll look at a
visual representation

00:26:33.930 --> 00:26:35.850
by pushing on the map button.

00:26:35.850 --> 00:26:39.330
In there, I can see all
the regions World Co is

00:26:39.330 --> 00:26:41.290
deployed all around the world.

00:26:41.290 --> 00:26:42.900
And if I mouse
over those regions,

00:26:42.900 --> 00:26:45.290
I can see the number of
users deployed there.

00:26:45.290 --> 00:26:47.970
1,005 in the west
and the east, which

00:26:47.970 --> 00:26:51.900
is 1,000 desktops and
five GPU workstations.

00:26:51.900 --> 00:26:53.970
Let's go take a
look at the users.

00:26:53.970 --> 00:26:55.100
Where are the users?

00:26:55.100 --> 00:26:56.850
Visually I can see
where they're located

00:26:56.850 --> 00:26:58.950
and how many there are
in different locations

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:00.250
of the world.

00:27:00.250 --> 00:27:02.430
We can also look at alarms.

00:27:02.430 --> 00:27:05.680
For any reason, if a user
cannot connect from anywhere,

00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:06.870
you'll see an alarm.

00:27:06.870 --> 00:27:08.940
Is it one user or more users?

00:27:08.940 --> 00:27:11.580
We have the visibility
across all of our customers.

00:27:11.580 --> 00:27:13.690
If a region of the
cloud goes down,

00:27:13.690 --> 00:27:16.260
we can see that across
all customers affected.

00:27:16.260 --> 00:27:18.810
Only Workspot has
that visibility,

00:27:18.810 --> 00:27:22.210
and it helps isolate the
actual cause of the problem.

00:27:22.210 --> 00:27:23.220
So there you go.

00:27:23.220 --> 00:27:25.920
Creating thousands
of new cloud PCs

00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:28.320
in multiple regions
for users anywhere

00:27:28.320 --> 00:27:30.250
in the world in minutes.

00:27:30.250 --> 00:27:32.130
As we scroll down through
the eastern region

00:27:32.130 --> 00:27:35.520
we can see all those new cloud
PCs fully provisioned, fully

00:27:35.520 --> 00:27:38.740
qualified domain names and ready
to go for each of the users.

00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:41.700
We can also go into the west
and scroll down and show

00:27:41.700 --> 00:27:43.830
all of those
additional cloud PCs

00:27:43.830 --> 00:27:46.260
ready for the users
in the western region.

00:27:46.260 --> 00:27:48.720
Ready for them to log in,
provision their desktop,

00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:50.050
and go to work.

00:27:50.050 --> 00:27:54.870
That's how it Workspot is simple
to deploy, scale, and operate.

